WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.020
Risk Profiler scores the fraud risk
of a claim, and explains every score.

2
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:09.822
Fraudulent claims leave insurers
with heavy financial exposure.

3
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.426
Reviewing every claim by hand is costly.

4
00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:15.060
And blanket approval
risks paying out fraud.

5
00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:17.607
First, it scores each claim.

6
00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.141
It explains how each fact moved the score.

7
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.738
And it reports on the case
in plain language.

8
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.677
A claim is described by ten facts.

9
00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.360
The model puts the fraud probability
at 35%.

10
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:36.462
That is below the 65% threshold,
so the risk is low.

11
00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:39.681
Now two facts change.

12
00:00:39.681 --> 00:00:43.707
The claim moves to a Friday,
and the driver has four past claims.

13
00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:52.477
82%. Above the threshold,
so the claim is flagged as likely fraud.

14
00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:59.006
Each bar shows how one fact
moves the score, up or down.

15
00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:03.377
The biggest push comes
from the four past claims.

16
00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.395
Green bars pull the score down.

17
00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:11.348
A language model writes
a short summary for the analyst.

18
00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:15.530
It names the four past claims,
and recommends further investigation.

19
00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:17.597
Risk Profiler.

20
00:01:17.597 --> 00:01:19.498
Fraud scores you can explain.
